# Evidence cards are sealed by SHA256 over their bytes, so the checked-out bytes
# must be identical on every platform. Without this, a Windows checkout under
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites LF to CRLF and every sealed artifact fails to
# verify. Measured on 5820ff3, all three sealed evidence cards mismatched in a
# Windows working tree while their LF blobs matched the recorded digests
# exactly, confirming line endings rather than content drift as the cause.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Font binaries carry the provenance work and must never be line-ending
# normalized; three of them legitimately contain CR bytes.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
